Hi all,

yes, it's me, and yes, it's about the office days again. Short version first, then the long version for those who like to find the catch.

SHORT VERSION
1. From Monday 4 November 2024 our core office days are TUESDAY and THURSDAY (not Tuesday and Wednesday as it says in Handbook v4, section 5.3 - this mail replaces that sentence).
2. Everything else about remote work stays as it is: max 2 remote days a week, max 8 a month, core hours 10:00-15:00.
3. NEW: the "hybrid week" (details below).
4. The home-office allowance goes up from PLN 60 to PLN 75 gross per month from 1 January 2025.

LONG VERSION

Why Thursday? Because the Wednesday all-hands turned out to be attended by about a third of the people it was meant for, mostly the ones who were in anyway, and because Rafał's sales team asked for a day when customers can be invited to Łużycka without the whole floor being half empty. Management Board agreed on 10 September. Marta's exact words were "fine by me, as long as the coffee machine is fixed by then", so if anybody has a spare engineer... Kamil, that is you.

The hybrid week. Once per half-year (January to June, July to December) an employee in an eligible role may work a whole week remotely: 5 consecutive working days, Monday to Friday. Rules, because there are always rules:
- request on form PD-12 (tick "HW") at least 10 working days before the Monday concerned;
- the line manager approves or declines in writing, and may decline for operational reasons but then has to offer the next available week;
- a hybrid week counts as 5 remote days and does NOT count against the 8-days-a-month limit;
- it cannot be taken by the Finance team in the month-end close window, which Priya has defined as the last 3 working days of a month and the first 2 working days of the next;
- the first hybrid weeks can be taken from 18 November 2024, and unused half-year entitlements do not carry over;
- operations staff on a shift roster are still not eligible (see 5.1), and before somebody from the night shift writes to me again: yes, I know, I read the comments, we are looking at something for the owls but it is not this.

Allowance. PLN 75 gross a month from 1 January 2025 for people who work remotely at least 4 days a month on average; the one-off equipment stipend (PLN 450 per 36 months) is unchanged. I know this is not a lot, it is what the budget allowed, and it is not an invitation to heat the flat with the server.

Parking. Because Tuesday and Thursday will now be the busy days: the car park at Łużycka has 46 spaces and we have a lot more drivers, so there is a lottery for permits on 25 October at 14:00 in the canteen. Permits are valid for one quarter. Cyclists get the shower key from reception, as before.

Questions to hr@korvane.example, please not to my personal inbox and not through Olek's group chat.

Ines

PS. The printer on the 3rd floor has been fixed again. This is not HR business but I was asked to say it three times.

